<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The window resizes from its authored size upwards, and never below it:
  every page is laid out for exactly this rectangle, so the authored size is
  the floor and the look at that floor is pixel for pixel what it always was.
  Above it, each page's lists, text boxes and bottom rows follow the edges
  they are anchored to.

  One caveat the client still owns: a page's own children are laid out on the
  frame that page is drawn, so a page never opened in this session and then
  resized past will lay itself out against the window's new size the first
  time it is opened: its rows keep their authored places inside a taller
  page. Opening a page once, at any size, settles it for good. This is a note
  for whoever fixes the layout pass, not something a plugin can work around
  from here.
-->
